</section></score></mdiv></body>
<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>When He, from His lofty throne,</l><l>Stooped to do and die,</l><l>Everything was fully done;</l><l>Hearken to His cry:</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>Weary, working, burdened one,</l><l>Wherefore toil you so?</l><l>Cease your doing; all was done</l><l>Long, long ago.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>Till to Jesus’ work you cling</l><l>By a simple faith,</l><l>“Doing” is a deadly thing—</l><l>“Doing” ends in death.</l></lg>
<lg label="5."><l>Cast your deadly “doing” down—</l><l>Down at Jesus’ feet;</l><l>Stand in Him, in Him alone,</l><l>Gloriously complete.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
